    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of the day at 74.61. His favorable matchup against Nick Martinez, combined with a significant +13% dynamic platoon boost and strong park factors, makes him our primary offensive engine. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **Zack Gelof** (67.85) also stand out as elite starts, both benefiting from soft matchups against pitchers with xERAs near or above 4.10, while **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.47) and **Bryce Harper** (65.00) provide high-floor production. **Yainer Diaz** earns a spot at 63.62, bolstered by an excellent matchup against Carson Whisenhunt, where wind conditions out of the park provide a slight nudge to his overall offensive ceiling.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gleyber Torres** (53.06) and **Justin Crawford** (52.68). While **Gleyber Torres** offers a higher base expectation, his negative platoon split against Tanner Bibee stifled his efficiency score just enough to keep him out of the starting nine. Similarly, despite the high premium we place on speed, **Justin Crawford** remains sidelined due to a combination of a lower-tier batting order position and a pedestrian matchup against Andre Pallante. We are exercising caution with **Cal Raleigh** today; while his score of 54.46 keeps him active, he carries a 31% rain risk, and we will monitor the weather closely as game time approaches. Finally, players like **JJ Bleday** and **Masyn Winn** have been relegated to the bench today, both falling below our mandatory 40-point efficiency floor due to difficult matchups against strong arms like Bailey Ober and Cristopher S\u00e1nchez.",
